From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 03:57:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Describe the RTC alarm

The J604 has no RTC alarm today (MEASURED on -8: rtc0 macsmc-rtc has
no wakealarm attribute), so nothing but the lid, the power button or
the keyboard can end a suspend-to-idle, and a timed wake (rtcwake, a
scheduled resume) is impossible.

The rtc-macsmc driver already drives the PMU's one-shot alarm when the
device tree describes its registers as nvmem cells and its interrupt
(Aurora 0d8a55c70a; T6030 uses it since 1d55fad4d3). Describe the
J604's: add the alarm cells to the main PMU's layout and give them, the
interrupt and wakeup-source to the SMC RTC.

Values from the J604's own ADT, /arm-io/nub-spmi0/pmu-main (abbey):
boot ADT (MEASURED, 2026-11-04 first-boot capture, sha256 e7af8fd7...)
and the j604ap 25G83 and 26B123 templates (SOURCE) agree:
- info-rtc_alarm_ctrl = info-rtc_alarm_event = 0x2000, with
  info-rtc_alarm_ctrl_en_mask 0x40, info-rtc_alarm_event_mask 0x02 and
  info-rtc_alarm_monitor_mask 0x01: the driver's RTC_CTRL_ALARM_EN,
  RTC_CTRL_ALARM_EVENT and RTC_CTRL_MONITOR bits;
- info-rtc_alarm_offset = 0x2008 (the 32-bit compare value);
- info-rtc_irq_mask_offset = 0x200e, info-rtc_alarm_mask 0x01;
- interrupt-parent = nub-spmi0, interrupts = <2 62>. As for the
  sn201202x controllers on nub-spmi-a0 (ADT hpm1 37/43/45 = their DT
  interrupts), the ADT number is the SPMI peripheral interrupt.

Which of the two PMU interrupts is the alarm is INFERENCE: 2, as the
T6030 description uses for its PMU's alarm. TO-VERIFY on the J604 with
an awake alarm (echo +10 > wakealarm, then the interrupt count and
the RTC_AF event) before any timed suspend test.

The probe disarms the alarm and clears a latched event (one write to
the control byte at 0x2000) before it requests the interrupt.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index c731686cfb..2a2e68d88e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -160,8 +160,13 @@
 
 	smc_rtc: rtc {
 		compatible = "apple,smc-rtc";
-		nvmem-cells = <&rtc_offset>;
-		nvmem-cell-names = "rtc_offset";
+		nvmem-cells = <&rtc_offset>, <&rtc_ctrl>, <&rtc_alarm>,
+			      <&rtc_alarm_mask>;
+		nvmem-cell-names = "rtc_offset", "rtc_ctrl", "rtc_alarm",
+				   "rtc_alarm_mask";
+		/* The PMU's RTC alarm: pmu-main interrupt 2 of nub-spmi0 */
+		interrupts-extended = <&nub_spmi 2 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		wakeup-source;
 	};
 
 	smc_hwmon: hwmon {
@@ -195,10 +200,25 @@
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
 
+			/* ADT pmu-main info-rtc_alarm_ctrl, info-rtc_alarm_event */
+			rtc_ctrl: rtc-ctrl@2000 {
+				reg = <0x2000 0x1>;
+			};
+
 			pm_setting: pm-setting@2001 {
 				reg = <0x2001 0x1>; /* DTV-PMU-3 */
 			};
 
+			/* ADT pmu-main info-rtc_alarm_offset */
+			rtc_alarm: rtc-alarm@2008 {
+				reg = <0x2008 0x4>;
+			};
+
+			/* ADT pmu-main info-rtc_irq_mask_offset */
+			rtc_alarm_mask: rtc-alarm-mask@200e {
+				reg = <0x200e 0x1>;
+			};
+
 			rtc_offset: rtc-offset@2100 {
 				reg = <0x2100 0x6>; /* DTV-PMU-4 */
 			};
